        <p><strong>2. Protect Your Digital Assets:</strong><br>
        While exchanges are convenient, for long-term storage of significant amounts of <strong>digital assets</strong>, a hardware wallet offers superior security. These physical devices keep your private keys offline, protecting your assets from online threats. (Example: Ledger or Trezor – <em>invest in a hardware wallet for robust security</em>).</p>

        <p><strong>3. Explore Decentralized Finance (DeFi) & Web3 Interactions:</strong><br>
        To truly engage with <strong>decentralized finance</strong> and the broader Web3 ecosystem, you'll need a non-custodial wallet that allows you to interact directly with dApps and DeFi protocols. These wallets give you full control over your private keys and assets. (Example: MetaMask or Trust Wallet – <em>your gateway to DeFi lending, DEXs, and NFT marketplaces</em>).</p>
